            <div xml:id="d502">

                <pb facs="0632" n="514" sameAs="frus:frus1928v02/pg514"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.512 Flour/32: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Minister in China</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">MacMurray</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1928-09-25T19:00:00-04:00"><hi rendition="#italic">September 25,
                                1928—7 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>327. In order that Department may inform interested parties telegraph whether
                    flour tax at Canton reported in Canton despatch 715, August 15 to
                        Legation<anchor n="72" xml:id="d502-f1"/> is actually in force. Also whether
                    Cunningham protested against flour tax at Shanghai (see your 597, August 3, 6
                    p.m.) and result if any of protest.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Kellogg</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
